Maia-3
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Maia-3 human-like chess models
    Copyright (c) the Computational Social Science Lab,
    University of Toronto
    https://github.com/CSSLab/maia3
    Licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3

Maia-3 provides both the opponents and the position evaluation. The
published PyTorch weights are converted to ONNX by
scripts/maia/export_maia_onnx.py and shipped in resources/engine/maia; the
web build additionally ships an int8-quantized copy of the same weights.

The conversion changes the file format and replaces RMSNorm with an
arithmetically identical decomposition so the graph exports at ONNX opset
17. The model itself is otherwise unmodified, and the export is verified
against the reference PyTorch implementation before it is written.

Note that the AGPL is more demanding than the GPL this application uses:
if you make a modified version of Maia-3 available to users over a network,
section 13 requires you to offer them its source. Shipping the desktop app
or serving the web build as static files is ordinary distribution and does
not trigger that clause.

